(5515261, 796211, 99506, '<td valign="top">A funny and interesting take on the challenge.<br/>Regarding the photography here are my comments.<br/> <br/>Watchout for distracting things in the background like the shower curtain and towel etc as it tends to <br/>draw the eye away from the main subject.<br/> <br/>I would be tempted to crop out the towel and more of the hand.<br/> <br/>Also I don''t know if you have photoshop but desaturating the yellow channel removes most of the shower curtain as a distraction.<br/>Now if that curtain is actually white then you may have a white balance issue in as far as it shoild be adjusted to suit the lighting condition, ie if you were using the regular lightbulb in the room simply set it to incandescent.<br/> <br/>Finally I don''t know if you intended to use a shallow depth of field but whilst the clippers are in focus the face of the victim lol is not suficiently out of focus to suggest to me at least that this was your intention.<br/> <br/>I had a quick play with it and am happy to send the result to you if you like.<br/> <br/>Anyway that''s my input  all the best with the challenge... 6 from me</td>', 'A funny and interesting take on the challenge.Regarding the photography here are my comments. Watchout for distracting things in the background like the shower curtain and towel etc as it tends to draw the eye away from the main subject. I would be tempted to crop out the towel and more of the hand. Also I don''t know if you have photoshop but desaturating the yellow channel removes most of the shower curtain as a distraction.Now if that curtain is actually white then you may have a white balance issue in as far as it shoild be adjusted to suit the lighting condition, ie if you were using the regular lightbulb in the room simply set it to incandescent. Finally I don''t know if you intended to use a shallow depth of field but whilst the clippers are in focus the face of the victim lol is not suficiently out of focus to suggest to me at least that this was your intention. I had a quick play with it and am happy to send the result to you if you like. Anyway that''s my input  all the best with the challenge... 6 from me', '2009-06-05 06:38:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(5515286, 795704, 32011, '<td valign="top">This is indeed a very powerful image.  At first I cringed at the cultural aspect of it, but on reflection, thought that it''s only the terrorist i.e. cowards that cover their faces in this way and thus realised the errors of my instinctive reaction.  The lighting here is excellent, as is the composition and sharpness.  I truly hope that this doesn''t suffer b/c of people voting on their initial reaction to this and stop and think.  Excellent photo.  Should do well.</td>', 'This is indeed a very powerful image.  At first I cringed at the cultural aspect of it, but on reflection, thought that it''s only the terrorist i.e. cowards that cover their faces in this way and thus realised the errors of my instinctive reaction.  The lighting here is excellent, as is the composition and sharpness.  I truly hope that this doesn''t suffer b/c of people voting on their initial reaction to this and stop and think.  Excellent photo.  Should do well.', '2009-06-05 07:39:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(5515288, 795835, 32011, '<td valign="top">Captain Morgans has to be one of the worst rums about... it is the enemy of the rum drinker.  I like the idea of linking alcohol and driving as enemies, so the idea is brilliant... but the keys are a little lost, the composition isn''t great, the shallow DOF doesn''t help the image, not does the lighting.  And what is that in the bottle (center bottom)?  Very distracting...</td>', 'Captain Morgans has to be one of the worst rums about... it is the enemy of the rum drinker.  I like the idea of linking alcohol and driving as enemies, so the idea is brilliant... but the keys are a little lost, the composition isn''t great, the shallow DOF doesn''t help the image, not does the lighting.  And what is that in the bottle (center bottom)?  Very distracting...', '2009-06-05 07:45:14.000000', NULL, 1),
