(5522100, 796127, 7342, '<td valign="top">FYI:  This was an opportunity shot while I was at lunch eating at a picnic table. This was not my car and it was not arranged, it was completely by chance.  It would have been awesome if there had just been one more 6 in the plate # though.  And this moth is quite large.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-06-10 01:35:00.</i></td>', 'FYI:  This was an opportunity shot while I was at lunch eating at a picnic table. This was not my car and it was not arranged, it was completely by chance.  It would have been awesome if there had just been one more 6 in the plate # though.  And this moth is quite large.', '2009-06-10 02:34:10.000000', '2009-06-10 02:35:00.000000', 0),
(5522101, 795790, 63503, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by basssman7:</b></div><hr/><i> ......... My other tip would be that shooting shots likes this from a lower angle gives them more impact and power.  Higher angles are more tame and less powerful. 5 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I am not sure this would be a valid rule, in fact the opposite may be true, especially when facial expression and head movement are the conveyors of impact and power, an example would be my ''brown ribbon deja vu'' image <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=763640" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/990/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_763640.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/990/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_763640.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/990/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_763640.jpg"/></a> which was inspired by a similar JL picture that was also taken from a high point of view.</td>', 'Originally posted by basssman7: ......... My other tip would be that shooting shots likes this from a lower angle gives them more impact and power.  Higher angles are more tame and less powerful. 5   I am not sure this would be a valid rule, in fact the opposite may be true, especially when facial expression and head movement are the conveyors of impact and power, an example would be my ''brown ribbon deja vu'' image  which was inspired by a similar JL picture that was also taken from a high point of view.', '2009-06-10 02:34:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(5522141, 795741, 54645, '<td valign="top">I too thought of Kierkegaard. The photograph is wonderful and moving. I would have scored it higher without the title which gives clues to your message. My interpretation is one of judgment, generalization, and stereotype, whether intended or not. But that''s art, open to interpretation and the personal journey through the piece. I had the same experience with the image that finished one space behind your entry. Such irony in a Jew finishing above the fellow in 13th place.</td>', 'I too thought of Kierkegaard. The photograph is wonderful and moving. I would have scored it higher without the title which gives clues to your message. My interpretation is one of judgment, generalization, and stereotype, whether intended or not. But that''s art, open to interpretation and the personal journey through the piece. I had the same experience with the image that finished one space behind your entry. Such irony in a Jew finishing above the fellow in 13th place.', '2009-06-10 03:14:16.000000', NULL, 0),
